    {
      "id": "UgwDb7eLBOyo50P5Mnl4AaABAg",
      "author": "@Geography.Secrets7",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/VByhxwyAODbU-juRPuJUDykPx9W70_Cx7gNtZIGzYTy3pTQkCnOcO2FflLTxkjpYB0FLAZ9ZQQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "I never realized how unusual Spain's geography is until I learned about Ceuta and Melilla. It's fascinating that an EU country has land borders in Africa. I recently put together 21 Geography Facts About Spain That Sound Fake, and the deeper I researched, the crazier it got",
      "likeCount": 2,
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-28T13:22:13Z",
      "replyCount": 4,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "UgwDb7eLBOyo50P5Mnl4AaABAg.AZo8a8wGAZGAa0lqWHcLtt",
          "author": "@jmtrevijano9160",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_mDOoLZ72SWSCEAH5NnnBRFvFhMs4sFKQsUqRhdqaE=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "North Africa is 14 kilometers away from mainland Spain and can be seen from the peninsular coast. It was ruled from Hispania (Spain) since the Roman Empire, 2000 years ago as the Mauritania Tingitana. Ceuta was ruled by the Kingdom of Spain before the Muslim invasion that came from Asia invading the whole of Christian North Africa. The Reconquista was not finished. What about Turkey and Istambul, the European a Christian Constantinopla? Or Russia both in Europe and Asia? What is extraordinary in it? It is not geography what matters, it is History.",
          "likeCount": 0,
          "publishedAt": "2026-08-27T16:55:30Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "UgwDb7eLBOyo50P5Mnl4AaABAg.AZo8a8wGAZGAa0jqOHARTX",
          "author": "@andresduque4128",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_nXer40dvTj75NcsTf7-3cprcDxEsO-OcwWXqRCIw45erv2=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "Proportionally, the territorial portion that once belonged to or was claimed by the Spanish Empire in what is now the United States would equal more than half of the country today, representing approximately 50% to 60% of its current land area",
          "likeCount": 1,
          "publishedAt": "2026-08-27T16:38:00Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "UgwDb7eLBOyo50P5Mnl4AaABAg.AZo8a8wGAZGA_VJVsleuCV",
          "author": "@jmtrevijano9160",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_mDOoLZ72SWSCEAH5NnnBRFvFhMs4sFKQsUqRhdqaE=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "Millenial History. Plus, Northern Africa is not at the other side of the Atlantic as America is. It is only 14 kilometers away and can be seen from the mainland coast of Spain. So Ceuta and much of North Africa was already ruled from Spain during the Roman Empire and later during the Hispanovisigoth Kingdom of Spain that was invaded at 711 AD by the Asian Muslim Arabs of the Caliphate of Damascus, who previously conquered Christian North Africa, and North African Berbers.",
          "likeCount": 0,
          "publishedAt": "2026-08-14T17:04:12Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "UgwDb7eLBOyo50P5Mnl4AaABAg.AZo8a8wGAZGA_P8_MaWAaA",
          "author": "@Iber73",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_my8fvElJjiNLz95tKDWw1iZA3WrFf0VLksrPqI4yFBXbFx=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "If you study the history of the United States, you will realize that Spain founded almost the entire American continent. All the most important and oldest cities and states are of Spanish origin; that is truly fascinating.",
          "likeCount": 1,
          "publishedAt": "2026-08-12T07:33:15Z"
        }
      ]
    },
